# Behaves like p_io (a ~3 ms burst of work, then a short wait), but the loop
# bound comes from a function call, which the classifier never evaluates. Even
# the counted-loop analysis can't see through it, and guesses 100 iterations
# where the truth is 10,000.
define limit with a
return a multiplied by 100
end
repeat 30 times
set n to limit with 100
set x to 0
while x is less than n
set x to x plus 1
end
wait 0.004
end
say "opaque done"
